Drahcir wrote:

> Anyway I've have two Artifacts (Mjollnir and Grayswandir) so
> far by sacrificing many monters and I've found an uncursed luckstone
> so I'm quite sure I have a very high luck.

An uncursed luckstone will raise your luck by three points on a scale
from -13 to +13 (giving it a value of +3, effectively). It will also
prevent it from changing automatically when time passes.

If you want your luck to get higher, you should #offer creatures at the
altar until you see four leaf clovers appear. After ten such clovers,
your luck will be at +13, and won't go down as long as you carry the
luckstone in your main inventory. Don't pray while you're trying to up
your luck.

> I'm currently burdened but I don't have anything that I can really
> spare. I've heard that you shouldn't become burdened as much as
> possible in one of the guides I've read.

I notice that you are making a classical beginner's mistake. You *think*
that there's nothing you can really spare. But you can.

For starters, find a chest or box or sack somewhere, put it next to an
altar or, lacking that, a staircase, and put everything that's still
unidentified inside it. Return there once in a while to put more things
in there. This is what veterans call a "stash". Use a chest to prevent
other creatures from using your scrolls, potions, and wands against you.

> I need to identify my inventory quick. What's the fastest way to do
> this? I don't have any identify scrolls on me.

There are no ways to identify your inventory quick (since you don't have
a blessed scroll of identify, which has a 20% chance of identifying
everything you are carrying visibly).

If you've found an altar yet, find out the cursed status of all your
things by dropping them on the altar (this will also work with
non-coaligned altars). Next, try on all non-cursed armour, pick the
best, and leave the rest in your stash.

For wands, engrave something with your fingers somewhere, then write on
the same spot with your unidentified wand. About 3/4 of all wands can be
more or less identified this way.

> I found a potion of water in a shop in an early level. I didn't know
> you could get unholy water before this, so I tried to make create
> another one and it turned in a uncursed murky potion. What would the
> murky potion be?

I'm not sure what you mean here. Could you be more clear?

Potions of ((un)holy) water cannot be changed into other potions, except
by dipping them into a potion of polymorph, which can change them into
*any* potion.

Dipping other potions into water will either curse or bless them (if
your potion of water was (un)holy), or dilute them (a second dip will
change them to water).

> If your inventory splits the same type of gems into two slots in your
> inventory does that always mean that one of those slots are real gems
> while the others are fake?

No. Both might be real gems, as well. There's only one type of *glass*
per color.

> Also when dropping them on to an altar it
> always gives an uncursed status to them. Is it even possible to get
> cursed or blessed gems? If so, why do they uncursed status to them?

Yes, you can find blessed or cursed gems, or bless or curse them
yourself. They're just very rare, and for game play, there is no
difference between blessed, cursed and uncursed gems whatsoever.

Note that load-, touch- and luckstones *do* behave differently for
various states of cursedness.

> How do I change my water into holy water? I have two bottles, one
> uncursed and one cursed. (Unholy water always cursed, right?)

Unholy water is just another word for cursed water, like holy water is
blessed.

> I tired to be pray with unholy one on the altar but didn't seem to
> work for some reason and I know what I have got plenty of luck.

You cannot pray very often. This is unrelated to your luck. If you want
to find out whether or not you may pray, #offer something. If you get "a
hopeful feeling" as a result, you may not pray yet. If you pray too
soon, it will take even longer before you may pray again.

Note that an altar must be coaligned to safely pray on one. Don't pray
at another god's altar!

Normally, when you drop potions of (unholy) water on an altar and pray
there, the potions will change into holy water, and the normal prayer
effects will also take place.

By the way, how do you know that your luck is high? Carrying an uncursed
luckstone will only increase it by three, and might even keep it down if
it was low when you picked up the uncursed luckstone!

> I've been lurking this newsgroup for a while now and it seems a lot of
> characters use different names for each of there characters. Is there
> any difference to gameplay if you use a different name?

When you get killed by (for example) a shopkeeper, there is a chance
that a "bones level" is created and saved to your disk. When you return
to that level with a next character with the same name, the shopkeeper
will assume it is the same character, and be hostile against that
character as well, even if you did nothing wrong.

> I have also heard a lot here about people saying that something is
> special about a lizard corpses. What's so special about them?

A cockatrice can turn you to stone. Eating a lizard corpse will stop
that process. Also, lizard corpses don't spoil, so you can take them
with you and eat them later, like lichen corpses.

> I've got a magic marker but I've never used one before. Is a magic
> marker any use at all for a Valkyrie? I've heard of the word
> 'Elbreath' but can't think of a reason why I would need to use it.
> All it seems to do is stop centain monsters for attacking just like
> pausing the game or can you use this to heal yourself for a while or
> something? Can a Valkyrie use these to make new scrolls?

You can use a magic marker to write on blank scrolls or spellbooks,
making them into useful scrolls. For example, write "enchant weapon" on
a blank scroll, and it now *is* a scroll of enchant weapon. For a
valkyrie, writing spellbooks is mostly useless, and note that you can
only write scrolls that you have already seen before in the game you're
currently playing (unless your luck is extremely high).

For "Elbreath", I suggest you read the Guidebook. It's spelled a little
differently, but searching the "Guidebook" file for "Elb" should be
enough.

No, I'm not helping you any more with this: EVERYONE should read the
Guidebook before asking questions here.

